name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q13_2025'

question 'How does the choice of field names in a schema affect AI-generated code?'

wrong 'It has no effect; the AI ignores the names and only looks at the data.'
wrong 'Field names must be written in a secret code to prevent the AI from understanding them.'
wrong 'AI tools prefer field names that are only one letter long.'
right 'Clear, descriptive field names help the AI "reason" about the data and generate more accurate logic.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 10

AI uses the context of names (like `user_age` vs `val1`) to understand the purpose of the data. Clear names reduce the risk of the AI "misinterpreting" the data and generating buggy code.
MARKDOWN
